{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-108826",
  "enisaUuid": "0a3e9c31-3ee2-33a4-b840-a5aac652ab62",
  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: avoid recursive multicast port cleanup\n\nbr_multicast_sg_del_exclude_ports() removes automatically added STAR_EXCL\nport groups by calling br_multicast_del_pg(). For S,G entries, that\ndeletion calls back into br_multicast_sg_del_exclude_ports(), so a large\nnumber of STAR_EXCL ports consumes one kernel stack frame per port and can\nhit the stack guard page.\n\nKeep the complete port-group deletion path for cleanup, but suppress the\nS,G exclude-port cleanup while that helper is already walking the same\nentry. Normal deletion callers retain the existing behavior.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 23, 2026, 12:21:31 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 30, 2026, 12:41:04 PM",
  "baseScore": 0.0,
  "references": "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ed8edcbcf2290dba13c1beeba27fc19ad38515b\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a7385f6605958aa69eeb185c91f45d77640d1e2\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26142868b0767e95e28b7a1237f58b292b54d1d9\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/695a5a4c69c922d9296b2d7ad5f1ce8c6858fc64\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fb87c6025f90191516bee3ce14b42eb3e1cfed7\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d109141ba14652146089ef78b32d5e4d5285ebad\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7931fb9181421953f3133b408b0f2e2b8dd68b61\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5158353121bae4f552cb677ce8c5c3ef52f93a0d\n",
